-- title:
--   The coherent cyclic compiler gives the uniform perfect-completeness reduction
-- statement:
--   The actual coherent-certificate compiler maps every polynomial-time uniform G₂ verifier family with completeness 2/3 and soundness 1/3 to a polynomial-time uniform G₂ family with completeness one and soundness at most 575/576:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{QMAClass}(\mathcal G_2,2/3,1/3)
--    \subseteq
--   \operatorname{QMAClass}(\mathcal G_2,1,575/576).
--   $$
--
--   Proofs in these classes are arbitrary density matrices. Uniformity is established for generators producing valid verifier codes on every input, including inputs outside the promise. This assembles the physical cyclic test with its actual finite-machine code generator.
